        "nl-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "499b5264-4f13-3e2b-821b-78925c3a624a",
                "word": "graagte",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ff7b8787-01b2-3ff9-a538-7781466e645f",
                        "entry_id": "499b5264-4f13-3e2b-821b-78925c3a624a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "genoegen"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee1d5490-9df3-4c62-9e62-b93a14aad0de",
                                "sense_id": "ff7b8787-01b2-3ff9-a538-7781466e645f",
                                "text": "Ook zij zagen in onze documentaire over de schaduwzijde van reislust vooral een aanleiding om zelf een aantal memorabele reizen te maken en gaven met graagte voorrang aan exotischer bestemmingen dan wat door de Nederlandse vvv keurig was uitgestippeld en bewegwijzerd."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8e04ac62-7eed-4ac1-b518-dc5819f35603",
                                "sense_id": "ff7b8787-01b2-3ff9-a538-7781466e645f",
                                "text": "Samsom verwijt VVD-fractievoorzitter Halbe Zijlstra dat die vaste contracten als een probleem ziet, flexwerk als de norm betitelt en werknemersrechten als ballast ziet. Dat is economisch kortzichtig, zegt Samsom. \"Ik weet het, de vakbeweging, de cao, het vaste contract, het wordt door rechts met graagte weggezet als ouderwets. Ik luisterde geamuseerd naar de ronkende teksten van collega Zijlstra op zijn partijcongres.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fa20b531-e2bc-4d9c-83d1-6d2aa87f7d58",
                                "sense_id": "ff7b8787-01b2-3ff9-a538-7781466e645f",
                                "text": "Zo duiken beide landen met graagte in de underdogrol, maar het feit is dat ze allebei móeten winnen. Voor Japan, vertelde De Wit eerder dit seizoen, is goud op het teamonderdeel misschien wel de belangrijkste schaatsmedaille van deze Spelen."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d8afd100-351c-4183-a505-61dbe4ffb99d",
                        "source_entry_id": "499b5264-4f13-3e2b-821b-78925c3a624a",
                        "source_sense_id": "ff7b8787-01b2-3ff9-a538-7781466e645f",
                        "source_sense_description": "genoegen",
                        "target_lang_word": "covetousness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "covetousness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ad39934-2e34-37b7-9c62-6ac9dc1a3cf0",
                                        "entry_id": "ff4c7187-3bb1-3bf6-8373-7822b1020ec2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Immoderate desire for the possession of something, especially for wealth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27d168b1-3967-43b9-a166-f6c8f2f2fae3",
                                                "sense_id": "3ad39934-2e34-37b7-9c62-6ac9dc1a3cf0",
                                                "text": "He which will yield to Fear. muſt neceſſarily yield to Covetouſneſs or any inordinate Deſire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ade1bdf3-53b3-4b46-bce0-b0930ca9f633",
                                                "sense_id": "3ad39934-2e34-37b7-9c62-6ac9dc1a3cf0",
                                                "text": "Covetouſneſs is the yelow Jaundice of the foul, which ariſes from the over-flowing of the heart with love to yellow gold, by which a Chriſtian is dull'd and deadned."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b52549ec-f66b-4575-90fd-75aa966b4191",
                                                "sense_id": "3ad39934-2e34-37b7-9c62-6ac9dc1a3cf0",
                                                "text": "Covetousness prevents all good, and is and inlet and encouragement to evil."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b510ebdb-7f96-458a-b139-5f5fd85a27b4",
                                                "sense_id": "3ad39934-2e34-37b7-9c62-6ac9dc1a3cf0",
                                                "text": "In obvious compensation and opposition the fear of nothingness becomes the source of covetousness..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d2c8459a-457c-40a0-b843-b25a7f437aa2",
                        "source_entry_id": "499b5264-4f13-3e2b-821b-78925c3a624a",
                        "source_sense_id": "ff7b8787-01b2-3ff9-a538-7781466e645f",
                        "source_sense_description": "genoegen",
                        "target_lang_word": "greediness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "greediness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "95d7859f-422f-39b9-81c7-8487d3aa8e71",
                                        "entry_id": "e66ff6fc-5f5e-3ece-a466-bb673954707c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being greedy; greed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88501a69-e290-4be2-9061-faf0a003c8b4",
                                                "sense_id": "95d7859f-422f-39b9-81c7-8487d3aa8e71",
                                                "text": "Thereto the body of a dog she had, / Full of fell ravin and fierce greedinesse […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7942c3b8-5b7a-4228-928b-4887cf1b84b0",
                        "source_entry_id": "499b5264-4f13-3e2b-821b-78925c3a624a",
                        "source_sense_id": "ff7b8787-01b2-3ff9-a538-7781466e645f",
                        "source_sense_description": "genoegen",
                        "target_lang_word": "appetite",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "appetite",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0b2f9625-1eeb-3264-be14-f29e543ccd31",
                                        "entry_id": "73d75e24-78e7-3c66-aaaf-0fa215845d58",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Desire to eat food or consume drink."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "713dae7c-6ca6-4c37-9939-7b685d1de061",
                                                "sense_id": "0b2f9625-1eeb-3264-be14-f29e543ccd31",
                                                "text": "The most rapid and most seductive transition in all human nature is that which attends the palliation of a ravenous appetite. There is something humiliating about it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53dc3eed-4fa1-40ca-a947-fce372f04cd0",
                                                "sense_id": "0b2f9625-1eeb-3264-be14-f29e543ccd31",
                                                "text": "And I return with an excellent appetite. There can be no question, my dear Watson, of the value of exercise before breakfast."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6aaee191-cee1-4d07-9daf-6a51bceb3ede",
                                                "sense_id": "0b2f9625-1eeb-3264-be14-f29e543ccd31",
                                                "text": "Though the breweries were forced to shut down, the dry spell did little more than whet the public's appetite for beer: Records show that within the first 24 hours after Congress lifted the ban Prohibition] in 1933, Americans guzzled 1 million barrels of the stuff."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0b49a88-cf7b-4c81-a9dc-8261e076e043",
                                                "sense_id": "0b2f9625-1eeb-3264-be14-f29e543ccd31",
                                                "text": "Biotics possess extraordinary abilities, but they must live with minor inconveniences. The most obvious issue is getting adequate nutrition. Creating biotic mass effects takes such a toll on metabolism that active biotics develop ravenous appetites. The standard Alliance combat ration for a soldier is 3000 calories per day; biotics are given 4500, as well as a canteen of potent energy drink for quick refreshment after hard combat."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "24217a58-2a8c-37d8-bb4f-c4dc4d5e80ad",
                                        "entry_id": "73d75e24-78e7-3c66-aaaf-0fa215845d58",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any strong desire; an eagerness or longing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "743721bb-3c02-4c18-91aa-c53af1104956",
                                                "sense_id": "24217a58-2a8c-37d8-bb4f-c4dc4d5e80ad",
                                                "text": "If God had given to eagles an appetite to swim."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "faec1c13-99b8-443a-b590-06f16054473f",
                                                "sense_id": "24217a58-2a8c-37d8-bb4f-c4dc4d5e80ad",
                                                "text": "To gratify the vulgar appetite for the marvellous."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "e9c34691-b493-3e1b-bb0a-c14e67ed6e6d",
                                        "entry_id": "73d75e24-78e7-3c66-aaaf-0fa215845d58",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The desire for some personal gratification, either of the body or of the mind."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "269f6782-9895-4b57-a11c-e47a8f4c24f6",
                                                "sense_id": "e9c34691-b493-3e1b-bb0a-c14e67ed6e6d",
                                                "text": "appetite for reading"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f66513a5-697e-489f-a008-e25bbd0f5ea6",
                                                "sense_id": "e9c34691-b493-3e1b-bb0a-c14e67ed6e6d",
                                                "text": "The object of appetite is whatsoever sensible good may be wished for; the object of will is that good which reason does lead us to seek."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "52581aa2-eef0-436d-ad7e-71d687f75da0",
                        "source_entry_id": "499b5264-4f13-3e2b-821b-78925c3a624a",
                        "source_sense_id": "ff7b8787-01b2-3ff9-a538-7781466e645f",
                        "source_sense_description": "genoegen",
                        "target_lang_word": "eagerness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "eagerness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "65d036ee-124b-3f8c-b46d-a8c89e4d7640",
                                        "entry_id": "c749c460-87a8-3acb-b319-2469dbdaf344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state or quality of being eager; ardent desire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0bc9350b-2d25-48f0-a508-71afffba8f03",
                                                "sense_id": "65d036ee-124b-3f8c-b46d-a8c89e4d7640",
                                                "text": "The things he had to tell about...were enough to make you almost tremble with excitement, when you heard all the intimate details from an animal charmer and realized with what thrilling eagerness and anxiety the whole busy underworld was working."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4f0137bf-0243-47cd-ad53-e92ecc29bf5e",
                                                "sense_id": "65d036ee-124b-3f8c-b46d-a8c89e4d7640",
                                                "text": "Meanwhile the larger company was showing no great eagerness to yield to the pressure of South Wales interests to convert its gauge, and with a view to forcing the pace, the Llynvi & Ogmore in 1871 promoted a remarkable railway from an extension of its system already authorised near Blackmill, eastward across country to join the Rhymney Railway at Nantgarw, in the Vale of Taff, above Cardiff."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "432658ed-9192-3e14-8f3b-7b855cbc3663",
                                        "entry_id": "c749c460-87a8-3acb-b319-2469dbdaf344",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Tartness, sourness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8eb665a3-d5b8-4f30-834a-8c2833c2209c",
                                                "sense_id": "432658ed-9192-3e14-8f3b-7b855cbc3663",
                                                "text": "Senvie, which is of a most biting and stinging tast, of a fierie effect,[…]serveth also to make a pretie dish of meat to be eaten, being boiled or stewed between too^([sic – meaning two]) little dishes in some convenient liquor, in such sort, as a man shall not feele it to bite at the tongues end, nor complaine of any eagernesse that it hath."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8fc85f11-962b-4b6d-8ae1-c1bf432d2884",
                                                "sense_id": "432658ed-9192-3e14-8f3b-7b855cbc3663",
                                                "text": "Presently the balsamick body is wounded, and turns sour sooner or later according to the degree of the motion; for this fierce motion or working wastes the pure spirituous Balsam, and awakens the original Qualities of Saturn and Mars, viz. an astringent Eagerness, or sour hard Quality, that would not have been manifested, if this irregular Motion had not excited it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e86700af-99c4-430e-98a1-d0c7af4b1133",
                                                "sense_id": "432658ed-9192-3e14-8f3b-7b855cbc3663",
                                                "text": "To this I answer that Beer nor Ale can be drawed off so fine from the Mash-Tun or Cooler, as to want a sufficient Sediment to feed it, as may be easily proved by an Observation when the Drink is drawn off, that never yet appeared to me without rather too much of this filthy Compound, which by its earthy and saline Parts naturally induces Hardness and Eagerness in the Liquor."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
